[require map::area::display [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a widget to show the information of a single [term geo/area] definition.

[para] The widget shows the statistics of the area, i.e. its center, number of parts, perimeter and
diameter, above a table of its vertices. Each row of the table shows the number of the vertex
(counting from 1), its latitude and longitude, the distance from the previous vertex, and the total
distance along the perimeter so far. A last row closes the perimeter, showing the distance from the
last vertex back to the first, and the total perimeter.

[para] The number of parts is the number of edges of the area, i.e. the number of vertices for an
area of three or more vertices, and one less than that otherwise.

[para] Distances are formatted for display with [cmd {map slippy pretty-distance}] of package
[package map::slippy].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::area::display] [arg pathName] [opt [arg options]...]]

Creates a new area display widget [arg pathName], configured with the specified options. The result
of the command is [arg pathName]. The command is also available as [cmd {map area display}].

[para] The widget initially shows nothing. Use method [method set] to show an area.

[para] The widget supports the following option:

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -on-selection [arg cmdprefix]]

A command prefix which is invoked when the user selects a row of the table. It is invoked at idle
time, at the global level, with one additional argument, the index of the vertex shown in the
selected row, counting from 0. Selecting the last row, which closes the perimeter, reports the
first vertex, i.e. index 0. The result of the command is ignored.

[para] Selections made through method [method focus] are not reported.

[para] The default is the empty string, i.e. selections are not reported.

[list_end]
[list_end]

The widget supports the standard methods [method cget] and [method configure], and the
following methods:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg pathName] [method set] [arg geos]]

Shows the area specified by [arg geos], a list of geo locations, i.e. latitude/longitude pairs,
the vertices of the area in order. This is the [const geo] element of a [term geo/area] value as
described in [package map::area::file]. An empty list clears the display.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg pathName] [method focus] [arg index]]

Selects the row with the specified [arg index] in the table, counting from 0, and scrolls the
table to make it visible. The row index of a vertex is its index in the list given to method
[method set].

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::area::display

map area display .area -on-selection {apply {{index} {
    puts "selected vertex $index"
}}}
pack .area -fill both -expand 1

.area set {{48.0 11.0} {48.1 11.0} {48.1 11.2}}
}]

[see_also map::area::table-display map::area::map-display map::area::file]

